                            <comment id="490447" author="JIRAUSER20212" created="Mon, 9 Mar 2026 15:38:20 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=adilger&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;adilger&quot;&gt;adilger&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=arshad512&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;arshad512&quot;&gt;arshad512&lt;/a&gt; I would like to share my thoughts on how to fix &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19944&quot; title=&quot;tunefs.lustre -V/--version cannot get the version sucessfully&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19944&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19944&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19945&quot; title=&quot;tunefs.lustre/mkfs.lustre -q cannot suppress output&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19945&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19945&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19740&quot; title=&quot;tunefs.lustre must protect against specifying multiple devices&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19740&quot;&gt;LU-19740&lt;/a&gt;. I hope we can reach an agreement on the approach and then move forward.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Current logic about the process of arguments:&lt;br/&gt;
1) Process --version argument and check if the last argument is really a device by calling chk_args().&lt;br/&gt;
2) Get the device by reading the value of argv&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;argc - 1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;
3) Process --erase-params argument in advance by calling getopt_long() for the first time.&lt;br/&gt;
4) Process other arguments by caling getopt_long() for the second time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I agreed that Andreas&apos;s patch is simpler to fix &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19944&quot; title=&quot;tunefs.lustre -V/--version cannot get the version sucessfully&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19944&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19944&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, but I think it is better to refactor the process of arguments before fixing &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19945&quot; title=&quot;tunefs.lustre/mkfs.lustre -q cannot suppress output&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19945&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19945&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19740&quot; title=&quot;tunefs.lustre must protect against specifying multiple devices&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19740&quot;&gt;LU-19740&lt;/a&gt;.&#160; For example, without refactoring, 1) we have to move `-q` argument into chk_args() and pick up it by doing a loop when fixing &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19945&quot; title=&quot;tunefs.lustre/mkfs.lustre -q cannot suppress output&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19945&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19945&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; because tunefs.lustre needs to supress the output of &quot;Read previous values&quot;. 2) we also have to check if muplite devices are specified by doing a loop when fixing &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19740&quot; title=&quot;tunefs.lustre must protect against specifying multiple devices&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19740&quot;&gt;LU-19740&lt;/a&gt; because tunefs.lustre should get the device in advance.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I hope we can simple the current logic like this:&lt;br/&gt;
a) Merge 1), 2) and 3) into simple_parse_opt() and make simple_parse_opt() can process any arguments which should be processed in advance.&lt;br/&gt;
b) It seems easier to maintain in the future if only getopt_long() is used to process all arguments.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
